	(text "Detector coupon: fast high/low capture (U40-U42). UNRESOLVED: not a validated 20 ns detector. Disconnectable at JP40 (input) and JP41/JP42 (outputs)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 30.48 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "76594f36-e38a-4c56-a2c8-b92483559bf0")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A; nothing here is simulated or measured)\nUNRESOLVED  Whole block. A coupon to capture the high and low levels of SDET so Control can derive a threshold; it is NOT a validated 20 ns precision\n            peak detector.\nPROPOSED    SDET -> JP40 (default: bridge) -> R150 49.9 ohm -> DET_IN. U40/U41 OPA356 unity buffers (+ = DET_IN, 200 MHz GBW, 360 V/us, SBOS212A p.3)\n            drive D40/D41 BAS70 into hold nodes CH/CL.\n            D40 anode at U40 output, cathode at CH (positive peak). D41 cathode at U41 output, anode at CL (negative peak). CH/CL: C150/C151 47 pF C0G\n            to GND, R151/R152 1 M to VCM_DET.\n            U42 OPA2320 (3V3): A buffers CH -> JP41 (default: bridge) -> VHIGH; B buffers CL -> JP42 (default: bridge) -> VLOW. TP40 CH, TP41 CL, TP42\n            DET_IN.\n            Footprints allow C150/C151 22-100 pF and R151/R152 0.5-5 M; pick by G2 test. The OPA356 input range is V- - 0.1 V to V+ - 1.5 V (SBOS212A\n            p.3), so U40/U41 are on 5V_A (3V3 would leave 1.8 V, too small for the SDET swing about 1.65 V).\n            Bypass at each OPA356 V+ pin: 100 nF 0402 + 1 uF + 10 uF (datasheet minimum recommended is 10 uF, p.10).\nKNOWN ERRORS (all uncorrected here): (1) Schottky forward drop about 0.3 V (BAS70, unverified at this current) makes VHIGH low and VLOW high by the\n            same amount; with a 1 M load it varies with level and temperature.\n            (2) Droop: CH/CL decay through R151/R152 with tau = 1 M x 47 pF = 47 us, so captured levels sag between peaks of a sparse 8b/10b stream.\n            (3) OPA356 output into the diode and 47 pF is untested for stability.\n            (4) Input leakage of the diode and U42 pins (pA scale) is negligible against 1 M but is not measured. (5) Hold buffers see no reset: the\n            level follows the data pattern, not the instantaneous eye.\nG2 TESTS    Compare VHIGH/VLOW against eye-histogram high/low levels over pattern density, bias and temperature; measure droop, drop, and added jitter\n            on SDET with JP40 closed vs open.\nALTERNATIVES  Two-diode (drop-cancelling) or in-loop (diode inside the amplifier feedback) detectors, a faster precision rectifier, or ADC capture in\n            the MCU (optional extra only; analog-first stays the baseline)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 30.48 185 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "220c73f6-d5f3-4159-886f-3a9740d0590f")
	)
